{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-187796-r4509873","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Hyderabadi Haleem (Ground Meat and Wheat)","sourcePageId":187796,"sourceRevision":"4509873","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-16T01:11:53Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Hyderabadi%20Haleem%20(Ground%20Meat%20and%20Wheat)&oldid=4509873","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:28.092Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using garam masala","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using lime","Category:Recipes using mutton","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using turmeric","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"9fdef782ec4bb8f01bad20d8dd50de1a58e2474bd83b1b19877a7384994c36c0","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = South Asian recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] whole [[Cookbook:Wheat|wheat]] kernels\n* 300 g boneless [[Cookbook:Mutton|mutton]]\n* 20 g fresh green Indian [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]]\n* 2-inch piece [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 6–8 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 100 g cooking oil\n* 3 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], finely [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 2 medium [[Cookbook:Lime|limes]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder (haldi)\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|garam masala]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste \n==Procedure==\n# De-bran the wheat, wash, and soak for 2 hours.\n# Grind the ginger, garlic, chilies, and salt to make a paste. Rub the mutton with the mixture, and [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]] for 1 hour.\n# [[Cookbook:Pressure Cooking|Pressure cook]] the soaked wheat and marinated meat for about 45 minutes. [[Cookbook:Mince|Mince]] and grind to a fine paste.\n# In a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]], heat oil, add the sliced onions. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] until brown, then add the spices.\n# Add the ground paste, and cook over low heat until the mixture leaves the sides of the pan, stirring occasionally. \n# Adjust the seasoning. Serve hot, with lime wedges coriander and fried onions as garnish.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using turmeric]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mutton]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Hyderabadi Haleem (Ground Meat and Wheat)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"200 g whole wheat kernels","sourceText":"200 g whole wheat kernels","amountText":"200 g whole wheat kernels","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"300 g boneless mutton","sourceText":"300 g boneless mutton","amountText":"300 g boneless mutton","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"20 g fresh green Indian chiles","sourceText":"20 g fresh green Indian chiles","amountText":"20 g fresh gree